It already is. That's why the vision system was
changed to reveal more of a lighted room, fanning
out on each side, as the PC approaches down a
hallway, and to show the parts of a lighted room
that should be visible, even at the far end of an
unobscured dark hallway. That is no particularly
great benefit to gameplay, just a change to make
NetHack work as physical reality works, on a basis
of "least astonishment".

Arguments persuasive to the DevTeam that NetHack
_unnecessarily_ departs from the laws of physics
have frequently resulted in improvements to the
game, as in the example of vision, above.

I suspect the DevTeam would consider "throwing a
rock by hand does more damage than throwing a rock
with a sling" to be an unnecessary departure from
physical reality, one which gives no gameplay
benefits by ignoring physical reality, and treat it
as a bug, were it filed as one.

